{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes","id":875126,"title":"Going Against the Steroetypes...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-26T19:19:20-07:00","id":875126,"title":"Going Against the Steroetypes...","content":"So... we all know that every splat basically has inherent incentives to play a specific way, with their powers, weaknesses, and so on encouraging that, basically attempting to guide you to a stereotype.<br /> <br /> My question is... how effective would they be at <i>not </i>being what they were meant to be according to the stereotypes?<br /> <br /> <br /> For instance, Werewolves are heavily melee monsters... so how good are they at NOT being that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:28:55-07:00","id":875134,"title":"","content":"Actually, they're expert hunters, really good at finding targets, harrying them by stripping them of advantages and pushing them into vulnerable positions, and finally dealing with them with surgical precision. Combat's kind of tangential for all but their specialists, who admittedly kill the fuck out of everything.<br /> <br /> So, how good are they at not being hunters?<br /> <br /> Well, as Blood Talons can attest to, their ability to be prey is both terrible and great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:35:52-07:00","id":875142,"title":"","content":"I've been itching to play a Gangrel who isn't a savage road warrior badass, but is instead a med student terrified of losing himself to Frenzy and violence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:42:23-07:00","id":875147,"title":"","content":"While they are hunters, I do think the <i>stereotype </i>is that werewolves are sort of uncivilized brawlers. I recall one of the complaints when people were trying to get people to note vote for Viking Werewolves in the Dark Era was that it was 'too obvious.' While probably the first thought to come to mind for most people at the thought of a pack is something like 'street gang.' There's also a tendency to believe they have an inclination to the wilderness, though just like some humans have never set foot outside of cities, either have some werewolves.<br /> <br /> Fortunately werewolves are just as at home being a part of the social elite, or intellectually bent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-26-2016, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:47:07-07:00","id":875151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=875142#post875142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been itching to play a Gangrel who isn't a savage road warrior badass, but is instead a med student terrified of losing himself to Frenzy and violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Done that with a botanist, was pretty fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Pay no attention to the man behind the Storyteller!&quot; <hr /><a href=\"https://www.fromdusktilljawn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">From Dusk 'til Jawn</a> - 2e nWoD game set in Philadelphia<br /> <a href=\"http://www.gravenlore.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Graven Lore</a> - 2e multi-venue nWoD game<br /> <a href=\"http://newhaven.mindrealms.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New Haven</a> - 2e nWoD game set in southern Maine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/951-caelene","name":"Caelene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:48:02-07:00","id":875152,"title":"","content":"I was one of those people who complained that it was too obvious, yes.<br /> <br /> So if the argument is just &quot;How good are they at not being a brawler?, the answer is &quot;Very good.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-26-2016, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:51:48-07:00","id":875156,"title":"","content":"It's more about being the exact opposite, sort of a silly question about being ironic....<br /> <br /> <br /> Still, this is an open question that goes for every splat and subsplat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:53:28-07:00","id":875158,"title":"","content":"Yeah, werewolves as prey. Better than you'd think, worse than the interested parties would like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:54:39-07:00","id":875160,"title":"","content":"Commenting to follow. Might contribute later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T20:04:39-07:00","id":875172,"title":"","content":"It's perfectly valid (and fun!) to go against the stereotypes, but your character should have <i>something</i> in common with the X-splat and Y-splay you chose.<br /> <br /> Let's suppose you're playing Vampire. You have Social Traits as your Primary for Attributes and Skills, but the Disciplines of the Nosferatu really appeal to you. This Clan's Bane gets in the way of social interaction, so you decide to keep your Humanity as high as you can. Your profession is counselor for humans and vampires alike, and you're a decent individual overall. Where's the hideousness that is part of the Clan? You can say that it manifests in the form of occasional possessiveness of the people your character helps. Sometimes, people say they feel ready to face life on their own, but your character is uncertain, and that turns into paranoia. We all fear being the target of an obsessive individual. It's intrusive and just plain creepy. <i>There's</i> your hideousness. You may not invest any dots into Vigor, but you will get a lot of mileage out of Nightmare and Auspex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T20:08:01-07:00","id":875176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=875142#post875142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been itching to play a Gangrel who isn't a savage road warrior badass, but is instead a med student terrified of losing himself to Frenzy and violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gangrels make fantastic detectives. I personally feel that using Prothean and Animalism to widen your investigation potential is much more fun than just spamming Auspex all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T20:18:34-07:00","id":875186,"title":"","content":"It's probably fair to say the stereotypical mage is a well-prepared scholar. While I know mages can have any occupation, how well do they fare when 'winging it?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T20:22:16-07:00","id":875192,"title":"","content":"Some Paths are better at it than the others. Obrimos and Mastigos can be careless all they want, their effects are pretty good even without preparation or thinking much. Thyrsus are also pretty good at improvising. Acanthus are...in the middle, and Moros definitely lose a lot without preparation, especially if you are Death focused; Death specialist is a minion master, and it's hard to do without planning and being one move ahead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T22:49:47-07:00","id":875328,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, a supernatural template's base abilities make them good at the things they're supposed to be good at as a baseline.<br /> <br /> Even a werewolf that starts with 2 Strength, 2 Dexterity, 2 Stamina, 0 Athletics, and 0 Brawl still forces Down and Dirty combat on many opponents, with a 4 dice pool and +2 weapon modifier. In regular combat they've got 3 turns of full lethal and bashing heals at 9 health, during which their opponents can't add Athletics to Defense. At the end of those 3 turns, they can either take 1 more turn and then risk Death Rage, or play it safe and &quot;just&quot; have 1 bashing heal per turn, 8 health, and a a 3 dice Brawl pool with a +2 damage modifier that automatically inflicts a Tilt on the first hit. Not <i>great</i>, but pretty damn good for a character with the minimum possible combat investment.<br /> <br /> A vampire with 2/2/2 in Social Attributes and 4 dots in Animal Ken with nothing in any other social skills can still manage a 4-dice pool at a Perfect Impression on <i>any</i> Social action against <i>any</i> human if they can manage to slip a drop of blood into their drink on three separate occasions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T00:10:50-07:00","id":875388,"title":"","content":"In 1E, I played a sexy Spring Ogre healer, an Ordo Dracul Gangrel researcher, a Mastigos martial art teacher. The Gangrel was the most challenging to play but even then it wasn't that hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T00:30:56-07:00","id":875400,"title":"","content":"I now want to play a Mage who's just a straight-up dudebro fratboy.<br /> <br /> <i>No one would see it coming</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T00:50:37-07:00","id":875405,"title":"","content":"Now this is not going directly against the template stereotype but rather the stereotype of the concept but a Nosferatu vampire still living in his mother's basement. So yes more or less a basement dwelling 'neckbeard' who was embraced and became a vampire.<br /> <br /> So the going against stereotypes here is that despite how he appears he is an ok guy. Without her knowledge he has been dosing his mother with vitae to halt the progress of [insert disease].","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T02:02:49-07:00","id":875437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=875400#post875400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I now want to play a Mage who's just a straight-up dudebro fratboy.<br /> <br /> <i>No one would see it coming</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't seem that unusual. Acanthus' tarot is The Fool. Which strikes me as very fitting for a dudebro fratboy.<br /> <br /> Just replace &quot;foolish&quot; with &quot;drunk&quot;. In fact, there's that classic saying &quot;God takes care of drunks and fools&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T06:38:44-07:00","id":875565,"title":"","content":"With beast, does going against the narrative go against the stereotype? .... or does going with the narrative go against the stereotype since beasts are meant to subvert the stereotypes of the narrative....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 04-27-2016, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T14:40:20-07:00","id":876000,"title":"","content":"Beasts subvert the monster's narrative by also being human, but they still often follow some stereotypes, like the seductive Makara or the rampaging ravager, and it could be interesting to play against those. You could be a scrawny Anakim nerd, or a Collector working at a charity for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T22:23:15-07:00","id":876286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=875400#post875400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I now want to play a Mage who's just a straight-up dudebro fratboy.<br /> <br /> <i>No one would see it coming</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages are connected with Academia, fratboys are obviously in college so they affirm only the stereotypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-28-2016, 01:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T22:44:49-07:00","id":876297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=876286#post876286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mages are connected with Academia, fratboys are obviously in college so they affirm only the stereotypes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fratboys (at least the ones you see in movies) are a corruption of academia. Rather than attending college to acquire knowledge, they attend college to get drunk and be douchenozzles.<br /> <br /> Maybe going with &quot;I wish to play a <a href=\"http://www.thefreedictionary.com/laddish\" target=\"_blank\">laddish</a> mage&quot; might be a better wording.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T02:05:51-07:00","id":876374,"title":"","content":"That fits right in with Mage then. Rather than acquiring knowledge to share with all humanity the Mysterium and Guardians lock it away from all but the &quot;worthy&quot;. The Silver Ladder are arrogant elitists. And so forth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T05:32:13-07:00","id":876507,"title":"","content":"So, then what about Mysterium who freely share secrets, Guardians who promote public and wanton use of magic, Silver Ladder oppressing or crippling humanity and other mages, Arrow cowards who don't fight, and Free Council close-minded tyrants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-28-2016, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T05:58:15-07:00","id":876537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=876507#post876507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, then what about Mysterium who freely share secrets, Guardians who promote public and wanton use of magic, Silver Ladder oppressing or crippling humanity and other mages, Arrow cowards who don't fight, and Free Council close-minded tyrants?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they really playable in long term? They defy they own Order missions...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T06:03:12-07:00","id":876545,"title":"","content":"I think the Guardians and Mysterium members would probably be shut down, the others likely just wouldn't be able to get very high in their organization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T07:49:48-07:00","id":876632,"title":"","content":"And don't forget the Seers, who are all about being privileged jerks who are there for power and getting away with enjoying the best out of life.<br /> <br /> Stereotypes are narrow visions that don't even apply to the games as designed. The stereotypical vampire is basically the spider in the web of contacts and social influence, but the Lance, Circle, Ordo and VII don't fit that stereotype in the first place. While Rahu and Irraka do tend to be &quot;melee monsters,&quot; the Cahalith, Itheur and Elodoth tend to have more social and mystical leanings, and often lack combat skills. The stereotypical mage is basically a wizard in their library (ie the Mysterium) - but that's only one of many Orders. Frankenstein is the sterotypical Promethean, but we can have golems and robots as well, who act nothing like Shelly's creation. And so on.<br /> <br /> Now, perhaps a better question would be &quot;how do we play outside of each game's specialty?&quot; Werewolves are hunters. Vampires use cooersion. Mages investigate. Prometheans evolve, changelings use illusions, hunters fight monsters, Bound serve as mediums and psychopomps, demons spy. Etc. If a vampire avoids use of any cooercive abilities, how well do they play? Well, pretty well to an extent - this is what a High Humanity vampire looks like, and playing one is highly rewarding if you like that kind of game. Mages that don't investigate? Less so - investigating strange things is the core of the game, so if you don't investigate, there's no game. Same with a lot of others. Playing against your specialty generally means you don't have any involvement in the plot of the games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T07:50:37-07:00","id":876633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=876507#post876507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, then what about Mysterium who freely share secrets</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Can't stop the signal&quot;? Wouldn't they just be pariahs of their Order?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=876507#post876507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guardians who promote public and wanton use of magic</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Idiots or Scelesti?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=876507#post876507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver Ladder oppressing or crippling humanity and other mages</div> </div> </div> </div>Seers?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=876507#post876507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arrow cowards who don't fight</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, this I could see if done like Flashman (or Ciaphas Cain)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=876507#post876507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Free Council close-minded tyrants?</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt this is actually under-represented. They probably just don't see themselves as close-minded, but Pride will do that to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=876632#post876632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And don't forget the Seers, who are all about being privileged jerks who are there for power and getting away with enjoying the best out of life.<br /> <br /> Stereotypes are narrow visions that don't even apply to the games as designed. The stereotypical vampire is basically the spider in the web of contacts and social influence, but the Lance, Circle, Ordo and VII don't fit that stereotype in the first place. While Rahu and Irraka do tend to be &quot;melee monsters,&quot; the Cahalith, Itheur and Elodoth tend to have more social and mystical leanings, and often lack combat skills. The stereotypical mage is basically a wizard in their library (ie the Mysterium) - but that's only one of many Orders. Frankenstein is the sterotypical Promethean, but we can have golems and robots as well, who act nothing like Shelly's creation. And so on.<br /> <br /> Now, perhaps a better question would be &quot;how do we play outside of each game's specialty?&quot; Werewolves are hunters. Vampires use cooersion. Mages investigate. Prometheans evolve, changelings use illusions, hunters fight monsters, Bound serve as mediums and psychopomps, demons spy. Etc. If a vampire avoids use of any cooercive abilities, how well do they play? Well, pretty well to an extent - this is what a High Humanity vampire looks like, and playing one is highly rewarding if you like that kind of game. Mages that don't investigate? Less so - investigating strange things is the core of the game, so if you don't investigate, there's no game. Same with a lot of others. Playing against your specialty generally means you don't have any involvement in the plot of the games.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about a non-Banisher that just wants to hide their head in the sand (but the circumstances and the Fallen World don't agree with them)? They <i>don't</i> investigate Mysteries, they get thrown into them and just try to survive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-28-2016, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T08:22:10-07:00","id":876653,"title":"","content":"Should we go looking for unusual stereotype then???.<br /> A vampire surfer bro, 'yeah missing the waves is harsh man, but, you know, you just got to be chill about it'<br /> A werewolf who wants to be a doctor. Takes strictly to the 'do no harm' oath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T08:39:09-07:00","id":876665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=876633#post876633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, this I could see if done like Flashman (or Ciaphas Cain)</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that's an Arrow heresy. You basically get kicked out, but people still come to you for advice if you're well known enough. Its already a well known phenomeon in the AA. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What about a non-Banisher that just wants to hide their head in the sand (but the circumstances and the Fallen World don't agree with them)? They <i>don't</i> investigate Mysteries, they get thrown into them and just try to survive. </div> </div> </div> That's a paradox, no pun intended. All mage powers revolve around investigation. If something happened to this non-Banisher, they would use their abilities to look at this mystery and figure it out to survive. The only way your suggestion is remotely viable is if our non-Banisher in question deliberately ignores anything that registers to his otherworldly senses, shuts his eyes and ears, and runs away all the time. At which point? That's going out of your way to avoid the game's plot. <br /> <br /> And that's not touching on how Obsessions and Consilium work. Mages literally have an innate drive to study mysteries and become addicted to them. Consilium are literally built around mysteries that mages gather 'round to study. If you don't want the mystery, you simply ask for help (other mages would love to study the mystery) and leave the city for somewhere banal. At which point, there's no plot anymore, and thus no game. You can't even argue that its one's destiny to be bothered this way, because a simple Fate 2 shield will protect you against that. A mage that wants to bury their head in the sand can pull it off easily.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, this is a thread about how easy it is to play against type. Your suggestion has nothing to do with playing against type, and everything to do with an ST forcefully creating an abnormal plot to enable this one thing. That's pretty much the definition of &quot;duper difficult&quot; if you have to design an entire <i>campaign</i> around one PC and try to shoehorn everything in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T08:48:57-07:00","id":876673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=876374#post876374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That fits right in with Mage then. Rather than acquiring knowledge to share with all humanity the Mysterium and Guardians lock it away from all but the &quot;worthy&quot;. The Silver Ladder are arrogant elitists. And so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, since when have Mages skipped classes (ignored Mysteries) to go get drunk (go get drunk)?<br /> <br /> <i>The sheer anti-intellectualism of the archetype is the point.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T09:22:44-07:00","id":876721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=876673#post876673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, since when have Mages skipped classes (ignored Mysteries) to go get drunk (go get drunk)?<br /> <br /> <i>The sheer anti-intellectualism of the archetype is the point.</i></div> </div> </div> </div> Seers. They're handed power and prestige despite not earning it in exchange for being part of a system of oppression and entitlement. Seers don't need to seek out mysteries, they're handed to them on a silver platter. Sounds like a match to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T09:30:46-07:00","id":876732,"title":"","content":"And how is the archetype of the fool not also anti-intellectual? Admittedly The fool is by nature, and the fratboy is by choice, but at heart both are a very anti-intellectual archetype.<br /> <br /> The fool says that luck and morality is superior to knowledge. The fratboy says that social skills and fun is superior to knowledge.<br /> <br /> <br /> A fratboy Mage would probably be pitted against a Dean Bitterman type; possibly an Seer worshiping the Unity, who emphasizes dull mindkilling rote learning. While the fratboy peruses mysteries that genuinely mean something to him but aren't taught in classes. Like how to brew magical beer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T09:37:02-07:00","id":876738,"title":"","content":"Or what Raven said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T09:56:44-07:00","id":876750,"title":"","content":"Except that's not really what the Fool represents in Tarot? It's not anti-intellectualism as much as naivete (remember that the iconic depiction of the Fool has him about to step off a cliff).<br /> <br /> But whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T11:48:27-07:00","id":876837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=876507#post876507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, then what about Mysterium who freely share secrets, Guardians who promote public and wanton use of magic, Silver Ladder oppressing or crippling humanity and other mages, Arrow cowards who don't fight, and Free Council close-minded tyrants?</div> </div> </div> </div>Those aren't stereotypes so much as the actual purposes of those Orders; defying that isn't exactly what this thread's about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T12:01:07-07:00","id":876851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=876837#post876837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those aren't stereotypes so much as the actual purposes of those Orders; defying that isn't exactly what this thread's about.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's considerably more to the Orders than the opposites of those. The Mysterium keeping all secrets isn't accurate, it's a stereotype, they are willing to share secrets if the circumstances are right, they've developed an entire subsystem for it, and their concern is about protection of magic. The Guardians also have the labyrinth, and are about more than simply keeping people from using magic in public.<br /> <br /> The stereotypes of the Orders winnow them down to their basics, a one line blurb. The Silver Ladder wants the best for humanity. The Arrow are brave warriors, and the Free Council open-minded democrats. True, at least to some extent, but not anywhere near the entire picture.<br /> <br /> That said, defying the actual purposes of the splat was brought up in the first response and has been a running theme through it anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T00:56:44-07:00","id":877442,"title":"","content":"How about instead of trying to avoid the stereotypes we twist them, approaching from the other direction.<br /> \u200bA Mage (or Mages) who have learned a terrible secret, a mystery that other Mages are seeking and now they have to protect it.<br /> A Werewolf who is being hunted by something that never attacks him directly, instead spreading its filth over everything around him forcing him to keep moving on even as he seeks a way to entrap his pursuer, a territory to claim in blood.<br /> A Sin Eater whos Geist doesn't care about ghosts, its one of the living it desperately wants to keep alive.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T04:56:15-07:00","id":877560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=877442#post877442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about instead of trying to avoid the stereotypes we twist them, approaching from the other direction.<br /> \u200bA Mage (or Mages) who have learned a terrible secret, a mystery that other Mages are seeking and now they have to protect it.<br /> A Werewolf who is being hunted by something that never attacks him directly, instead spreading its filth over everything around him forcing him to keep moving on even as he seeks a way to entrap his pursuer, a territory to claim in blood.<br /> A Sin Eater whos Geist doesn't care about ghosts, its one of the living it desperately wants to keep alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) GotV or Myst, take your pick. Just because you study mysteries doesn't mean that you have to share it. Or don't count as a mystery yourself for others to study.<br /> 2) That could be any of the five sacred prey or one of the Idigam, depending on how the ST runs it. Flipping predator-prey rolls is common in Werewolf games. As well, this is not a character concept. This is an ST plot. We should be talking about character concepts that don't requite STs to run very specific plots to get an &quot;anti-stereotype&quot; game. If you want to talk about non-stereotypical plots, that's a different subject.<br /> 3) Celebrant Archetype. Many geister don't care about ghosts. The Bound often end up dealing with ghosts because its the only way to get peace from all the undead bothering you. Its not a duty, its something that happens because you're nagged to death (ha!)<br /> <br /> <br /> Stereotypes are narrow, and the books are very good with portraying a wide variety of character archetypes, including the playing-against-type. Sure, you can eventually come up with a concept that defies the archetype the books are meant to cover completely. That said? It usually involves a character that is deliberately incompetent and has no drive to get involved in the actual plot, which is pretty much a mean move as a player. You want to work together with the ST on plot, not against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-29-2016, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T05:16:16-07:00","id":877576,"title":"","content":"Here's one.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure one of the most common stereotypes for mages is that they're all-powerful. Before this starts into an argument, lets remember stereotypes are not always correct. It's just something <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/839568-convince-me-mage-supremacy-isn-t-what-i-should-be-seeing\">some people believe.</a><br /> <br /> So how would mages fare if they only had mage sight and mage armor? For their sake you can use the second edition rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-29-2016, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T06:30:10-07:00","id":877628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=877576#post877576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's one.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure one of the most common stereotypes for mages is that they're all-powerful. Before this starts into an argument, lets remember stereotypes are not always correct. It's just something <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/839568-convince-me-mage-supremacy-isn-t-what-i-should-be-seeing\">some people believe.</a><br /> <br /> So how would mages fare if they only had mage sight and mage armor? For their sake you can use the second edition rules.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For lack of a better way of saying it, they'd be absolutely buggered. Mage sight is fantastic at detecting things and investigating, mage armour can let you survive a lot, but without any of the other powers they have access to they'd be a mortal with a bit of fuel to let them discover things or survive a bullet a bit more easily. Going up against another template they'd either have to be as ingenious as a hunter who has managed to survive at tier 1 for years, or they would die a little better informed about the symbols that make up whatever they're up against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T07:33:15-07:00","id":877663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=877628#post877628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> For lack of a better way of saying it, they'd be absolutely buggered. Mage sight is fantastic at detecting things and investigating, mage armour can let you survive a lot, but without any of the other powers they have access to they'd be a mortal with a bit of fuel to let them discover things or survive a bullet a bit more easily. Going up against another template they'd either have to be as ingenious as a hunter who has managed to survive at tier 1 for years, or they would die a little better informed about the symbols that make up whatever they're up against.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, it's fully possible, is what you are saying? Some thought needs to be put into <i>why</i> they never develop their Arcana, but as a character, it seems valid. Maybe they are a Banisher who tries to reject magic completely (unlike the common hypocrite Banishers)?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T11:22:29-07:00","id":877914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes#post875126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... we all know that every splat basically has inherent incentives to play a specific way, with their powers, weaknesses, and so on encouraging that, basically attempting to guide you to a stereotype.<br /> <br /> Mage has now been cleared for release, so...Next Wednesday good for everyone?<br /> My question is... how effective would they be at <i>not </i>being what they were meant to be according to the stereotypes?<br /> <br /> <br /> For instance, Werewolves are heavily melee monsters... so how good are they at NOT being that?</div> </div> </div> </div>My two cents would be: whatever it takes to make a good story but don't go against the mood lest you'll destroy the raison d'etre of those splats","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T00:55:43-07:00","id":878578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=877663#post877663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, it's fully possible, is what you are saying? Some thought needs to be put into <i>why</i> they never develop their Arcana, but as a character, it seems valid. Maybe they are a Banisher who tries to reject magic completely (unlike the common hypocrite Banishers)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, it's fully possible for them to go up against the other splats. Unless they're teamed up with like-minded people to take on the other splat, they'll likely die, but it's fully possible. At the point where they've got mage sight and mage armour only, they're just hunters who can spot other supernaturals a bit better and would maybe take an extra turn or two to kill. And hunters aren't exactly known for surviving things very long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T01:17:32-07:00","id":878590,"title":"","content":"Well, they don't have to kill, or 'go up against' other splats. Mage sight would still allow them to investigate and study things.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to associate them with Hunter they would be more in the vein of Network Zero, or a non-scientific Null Mysteriis. Probably with a bit of Aegis Kai Doru mixed in, not for the slaying, but for the artifact collecting and studying. Through their studies they would probably know a lot about banes and bans, and be ready to take advantage of them, as they seem to be something almost everything supernatural has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-30-2016, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T01:25:08-07:00","id":878596,"title":"","content":"There's also small scale Tier 1 mysteries that a sight&amp;armour-only Mage might investigate. A Rank 1/2 ghost for example, a mortal with a psychic merit.<br /> <hr /><br /> An idea I had for a non-steryotypical Beast would be one who has a policy of only feeding his Hunger with food freely offered, never directly intervening. An example might be a war correspondent who feeds his Hunger for Ruin just by being near the fighting. Or perhaps one who has a Chamber both at home and in the Gaza Strip. When his Satiety drops down to 5 he detours through the Dream and waits for food to turn up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T04:40:41-07:00","id":878659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=877663#post877663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, it's fully possible, is what you are saying? Some thought needs to be put into <i>why</i> they never develop their Arcana, but as a character, it seems valid. Maybe they are a Banisher who tries to reject magic completely (unlike the common hypocrite Banishers)?</div> </div> </div> </div> The concept isn't not developing Arcana, but not using the Arcana. That's pretty much the definition of a high-Wisdom character, using only the minimum of magic. From an in game perspective, using Mage Sight all the time should lead to an increase in your Gnosis and Arcana rating.<br /> <br /> Honestly, why are we so hyper focused on Mage? There ARE other games. Why not discuss Beast or Demon or Promethean or Changeling or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T09:45:45-07:00","id":878812,"title":"","content":"I can't think of any worthwhile stereotypes for most of those. No need to be defensive, there's no 'hyper focus' it just came up twice.<br /> <br /> What if Changelings had a great time in Arcadia? Then they would spend their lives trying to find their way back. Or wouldn't escape at all.<br /> <br /> What if Beasts didn't scare people? Then they don't scare people, their Horrors go AWOL and feed themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-30-2016, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T12:48:28-07:00","id":878936,"title":"","content":"The way I see it is that the counter stereotype for a Beast would be that instead of the Monster that scares other you would be a victim from horrors, in other word, changeling.<br /> As for changeling instead of the abused victim you would be the abuser, so in other word a Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T12:53:58-07:00","id":878942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=878936#post878936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for changeling instead of the abused victim you would be the abuser, so in other word a Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, y'know, an Icebound Duke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T13:17:10-07:00","id":878960,"title":"","content":"Regarding Beasts, isn't it the usual conceit that the Horror make the Beast a monster and drives them to inflict terror? What if it's the <i>human</i> that's worse and the Horror is actually a positive influence? (Though I'm doubting this would really work...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T13:28:30-07:00","id":878968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=878960#post878960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Beasts, isn't it the usual conceit that the Horror make the Beast a monster and drives them to inflict terror? What if it's the <i>human</i> that's worse and the Horror is actually a positive influence? (Though I'm doubting this would really work...)</div> </div> </div> </div> A Nemesis who's Devouring has changed them from a mindless rebel into someone who genuinely tries to strike out at the sources of corruption and tyranny, perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T22:46:00-07:00","id":879301,"title":"","content":"You know what, I'ma just C&amp;P from a conversation I had else where, I might build on it later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's not how the world works. And while it's a bit misleading to word it this way, Beasts are the world.<br /> <br /> I need to switch loads, and then I'll comment.<br /> <br /> But like.<br /> <br /> You don't ask a storm kindly if it can wreck your house.<br /> <br /> You don't ask a swarm of crows to only steal your stuff when you're ready.<br /> <br /> You don't ask the night to just wait a few second before being dark.<br /> <br /> As a Beast, you are not your own person anymore. You are the world as humanity sees it.<br /> <br /> You are Nature, the Base, the Instinctive and Intuitive.<br /> <br /> You are the Bitch Goddess.<br /> <br /> Like, why do people think the Primordial Dream is nudged RIGHT THE FUCK UP against the Anima Mundi?<br /> <br /> It's not just there for shits and giggles. </div> </div> </div>You're metaphysical nature as a Beast is not kindness. You cannot feed by politely intervening. You feed by being the world. You <i>exist</i> when you behave as the world. You <i>be </i>when you violate and shock and panic and fear and <i>reveal</i> <i>all the ways that the species is never really safe, is never really bigger than they were when they first stood up</i>.<br /> <br /> Kindness and individuality are pursuits that come second to the fact that <i>this is who you are now</i>. You're <i>the world</i>. And you will <i>die</i> if you pretend that the world is anything other than what it is.<br /> <br /> <i>This is what it means to be Primordial.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-01-2016, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T03:32:14-07:00","id":879420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=879301#post879301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't ask a storm kindly if it can wreck your house.</div> </div> </div> </div> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/zVdlg4OXqNI?t=7m\" target=\"_blank\">We don't</a>? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T15:11:22-07:00","id":884938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=879301#post879301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your metaphysical nature as a Beast is not kindness. You cannot feed by politely intervening. You feed by being the world. You <i>exist</i> when you behave as the world. You <i>be </i>when you violate and shock and panic and fear and <i>reveal</i> <i>all the ways that the species is never really safe, is never really bigger than they were when they first stood up</i>.<br /> <br /> Kindness and individuality are pursuits that come second to the fact that <i>this is who you are now</i>. You're <i>the world</i>. And you will <i>die</i> if you pretend that the world is anything other than what it is.<br /> <br /> <i>This is what it means to be Primordial.</i></div> </div> </div> </div> So, you agree with what the Joker is saying (not necessarily what he's doing) in <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oowR5vL6oPM\" target=\"_blank\"><b>this video</b></a>?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T15:39:06-07:00","id":884955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=884938#post884938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, you agree with what the Joker is saying (not necessarily what he's doing) in <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oowR5vL6oPM\" target=\"_blank\"><b>this video</b></a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Well, yeah. Why wouldn't anyone agree with him? Get the most out of life while it's here. Even killers can speak ancient wisdoms. That's stuff I learned in the first grade.<br /> <br /> BUT!<br /> <br /> 2)That's not the point I was making, and in fact it's something of a far afield thing. So, first off, I actually approve of the teaching culture, and in fact call it the most logical, ethical, and moral thing you can ask of a Beast to do in relation to their nature.<br /> <br /> But that said, there's that nature. It isn't kind. Hurricanes don't stop, predators don't question, night doesn't slow, instincts don't leave. The Horrors of the Primordial Dream are, first, the fear of the uncaring world, second, the naming of said fears, and third, the 'conquest' of the world(Maybe, that becomes complicated, not important for the moment). The point made was that a Beast's existence <i>is</i> violation, they have to, it's what they are. They derive sustenance-<i>existence-</i>from the fact that mankind is afraid of the world.<br /> <br /> It obviates the point to try and eat only what's freely offered. That's not the way the world works, and therefore that idea can never feed a Beast.<br /> <br /> A Beast can frame it in such a way that teaches, that enlightens, that reveals silver linings after the fact, but The Beast Must Violate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:35:59-07:00","id":884998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=884955#post884955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Well, yeah. Why wouldn't anyone agree with him? Get the most out of life while it's here. Even killers can speak ancient wisdoms. That's stuff I learned in the first grade.<br /> <br /> BUT!<br /> <br /> 2)That's not the point I was making, and in fact it's something of a far afield thing. So, first off, I actually approve of the teaching culture, and in fact call it the most logical, ethical, and moral thing you can ask of a Beast to do in relation to their nature.<br /> <br /> But that said, there's that nature. It isn't kind. Hurricanes don't stop, predators don't question, night doesn't slow, instincts don't leave. The Horrors of the Primordial Dream are, first, the fear of the uncaring world, second, the naming of said fears, and third, the 'conquest' of the world(Maybe, that becomes complicated, not important for the moment). The point made was that a Beast's existence <i>is</i> violation, they have to, it's what they are. They derive sustenance-<i>existence-</i>from the fact that mankind is afraid of the world.<br /> <br /> It obviates the point to try and eat only what's freely offered. That's not the way the world works, and therefore that idea can never feed a Beast.<br /> <br /> A Beast can frame it in such a way that teaches, that enlightens, that reveals silver linings after the fact, but The Beast Must Violate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, Beasts can polish the turd of their nature until it is gleaming, but it remains a turd?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:47:57-07:00","id":885008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=884998#post884998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So, Beasts can polish the turd of their nature until it is gleaming, but it remains a turd?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it doesn't quite capture the tenor that's appropriate for Beast, because Beasts <i>can</i> use their Hunger to help the human species smarter, wiser, kinder, braver, more humble, etc, and in so doing transform their nature into a valuable crucible.<br /> <br /> But they do still have to kick the door down. So, you know. Small measures of truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T17:06:09-07:00","id":885017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=884998#post884998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Beasts can polish the turd of their nature until it is gleaming, but it remains a turd?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=885008#post885008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think it doesn't quite capture the tenor that's appropriate for Beast, because Beasts <i>can</i> use their Hunger to help the human species smarter, wiser, kinder, braver, more humble, etc, and in so doing transform their nature into a valuable crucible.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But they do still have to kick the door down. So, you know. Small measures of truth.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I am not afraid of turds. I am afraid of wolves. And while wolves can learn who and when to bite, they cannot learn to never bite. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T17:26:04-07:00","id":885027,"title":"","content":"You can use it to chop wood or to cleave a skull in half, but an axe is an axe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T18:41:44-07:00","id":885071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=885017#post885017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am not afraid of turds. I am afraid of wolves. And while wolves can learn who and when to bite, they cannot learn to never bite.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousCrhistian240</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">You can use it to chop wood or to cleave a skull in half, but an axe is an axe.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">THese are better, yes.<br /> <br /> EDIT: You can use a hammer and chisel to make a statue or to destroy a statue, but either way you're breaking stone.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T19:05:11-07:00","id":885082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=885071#post885071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">THese are better, yes.<br /> <br /> EDIT: You can use a hammer and chisel to make a statue or to destroy a statue, but either way you're breaking stone.</span></div> </div> </div> </div> I remembered <a href=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/04/d7/af/04d7afa162ae3cbbcf5d994aae2cdfb1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><b>another analogy.</b></a> <br /> <br /> I better stop here before I feel like a Philosophy Major. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T19:21:32-07:00","id":885088,"title":"","content":"uhafaproblamwitphilosophymajors?<br /> <br /> (Pff, like I'm one to talk, I have an English Major.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T19:22:06-07:00","id":885091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=878812#post878812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't think of any worthwhile stereotypes for most of those. No need to be defensive, there's no 'hyper focus' it just came up twice.<br /> <br /> What if Changelings had a great time in Arcadia? Then they would spend their lives trying to find their way back. Or wouldn't escape at all.<br /> <br /> What if Beasts didn't scare people? Then they don't scare people, their Horrors go AWOL and feed themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not even hard, in fact:<br /> <br /> -A Changeling could be taken as a part of a pact with a Gentry for a limited time, then booted out of Arcadia where they lived in a paradise. The Changeling could then be trying to get back to this specific Realm while dodging Hunters or the pact cold forbid them to ever go back and they would have to integrate in Lost society where they'd be forever unable to completely relate to the Changelings who suffered from their durance.<br /> <br /> -A Beast could rely on Family Banquet to feed, never directly scaring anyone, building a Kinship network to keep themselves well fed, taking the role of broker, monster for hire, supernatural kingpin or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T19:40:06-07:00","id":885105,"title":"","content":"I think we're having a problem of understanding just what stereotypes we're breaking here. It's turned into an argument about critter's nature, and a lot of the answers often end up fulfilling nature rather than defying stereotype.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Like, as an example, the stereotype of werewolves as fight masters and brawlers and such, that's countered by the Iron Master who is an adept hunter without ever having an idea of how to throw a punch. But you try and argue against them choosing not to be hunters, and it just doesn't work on virtue of a slippery slope.<br /> <br /> A stereotype of Beast is that they are inherently evil people who can only ruin lives, which is countered by the Tyrant who uses his power to increase the reach and improve the facilities of various homeless shelters and suicide support programs, the Nemesis who reins in her fellow monsters and keeps them from acting carelessly.<br /> <br /> I think this was what we were going for originally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-07-2016, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T20:28:01-07:00","id":885129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/875126-going-against-the-steroetypes?p=885105#post885105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we're having a problem of understanding just what stereotypes we're breaking here. It's turned into an argument about critter's nature, and a lot of the answers often end up fulfilling nature rather than defying stereotype.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Like, as an example, the stereotype of werewolves as fight masters and brawlers and such, that's countered by the Iron Master who is an adept hunter without ever having an idea of how to throw a punch. But you try and argue against them choosing not to be hunters, and it just doesn't work on virtue of a slippery slope.<br /> <br /> A stereotype of Beast is that they are inherently evil people who can only ruin lives, which is countered by the Tyrant who uses his power to increase the reach and improve the facilities of various homeless shelters and suicide support programs, the Nemesis who reins in her fellow monsters and keeps them from acting carelessly.<br /> <br /> I think this was what we were going for originally.</div> </div> </div> </div> How about a Collector who works as a spy or some other type of intelligence gatherer for their country? They can do heinous things frequently in the name of protecting their nation's sovereignty. To other nations, they are a living boogeyman. Their compatriots think of them as symbol of the nation's cunning and might. Should they inspire a spy from a rival nation to become a Hero, the same story would be told.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-07-2016, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}